I replaced the indexed loop with a range-based loop so the vector bounds are evaluated once and the repeated `size()`/`int` cast and `operator[]` overhead are removed while preserving first-match semantics.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    for (Field& field : fields)
    {
        if (field.GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return &field;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```